# `||` right before an operator is two pipes, not C's `or`: DS0103.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' || take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..23
  PIPELINE@0..22
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE2@13..15 "||"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    TAKE_OP@16..22
      IDENT@16..20 "take"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      LITERAL@21..22
        LONG@21..22 "5"
  WHITESPACE@22..23 "\n"

error[DS0103]: two `|` in a row
  --> query:1:14
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' || take 5
  |              ^^ one `|` is enough
  |
  = help: remove the extra `|`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | take 5
which parses without errors
